      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T17:19:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `servo_bridge_pop_tx_frame()` pops a `SERVO_FRAME_MSC_DATA (0x90)` frame into `bridge_to_usart4`, it immediately clears `n-\u003epending_msc_len \u003d 0U` without credit flow control or per-chunk/per-sector ACK, allowing `bridge_arbiter_deferred()` (`usb_bridge.c:634`) to immediately consume the next `EP2 OUT` packet. During a 512-byte sector read (9 frames \u003d 585 UART wire bytes), all 585 bytes are streamed back-to-back at 1.000 Mbps (~5.85 ms) into the ATmega32U4\u0027s 256-byte `UartRx_Buffer`, which will overflow whenever `Bridge_Task()` on the ATmega32U4 is busy for \u003e2.56 ms.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "80b5532ccc31156bf4be4b2154dd9df12bc6a59e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
